      "ChannelId": "UCiZeuI-7OPs7TmMel6Q5Msw",
      "ChannelTitle": "Kanishk Nishar",
      "Description": "Los Angeles Philharmonic Orchestra; Otto Klemperer, conductor\nConcert of 1 January 1934, Civic Auditorium, Pasadena, California\n\nElectro-Vox originally re-mastered this from the original discs, and it was released on CD in the 1990s by Archiphon but seems to have been out of print for many years. It\u2019s Klemperer\u2019s first recording after he fled Europe, his first live recording, and his second and last recording of music by Verdi. (He recorded Desdemona\u0027s Ave Maria, from Otello, with Rose Ader in Berlin in 1931.)\n\nRadio announcement (0:00)\n\nGiuseppe Verdi. I vespri siciliani\nOverture (0:35)\n\nRadio announcement (The announcer appears to confuse the Fifth and Sixth Symphonies) (8:05)\n\nLudwig van Beethoven. Symphony no. 5 in C minor, op. 67\nI. Allegro con brio (8:51)\nII. Andante con moto (16:29)\nIII. Allegro (26:15) -\nIV. Allegro (31:15)\n\nRadio announcement (The announcer pronounces the title peculiarly as \u201CDie Meisterzinger,\u201D e.g., -tsinger.) (41:10) \n\nRichard Wagner die Meistersinger von N\u00FCrnberg\nAct I. Vorspiel (42:02)",
      "PlaylistId": "PL1zgNCoWt_7ZSiF--ol6_fIl7R_YRe_hI",
